   "status": "proposal",
   "heading": "Validation page proposal (winner p-100; content only, NOT deployed)",
   "markdown": "**Headline (a complainer's own words):**\n> \"When there are changes to the games, why in the heck doesn’t the app tell me? I have to check it manually constantly.\"\n\n**Subhead:** Every kid, every team app, one schedule. Paste each team's calendar link once and get a push the moment a game moves. Works on Android, iPhone and the web.\n\n**3 benefits**\n1. **All teams in one place.** TeamSnap, GameChanger, SportsEngine, Heja and more, color-coded by kid, right in the calendar you already use.\n2. **Know the second a game moves.** A push alert when a game or practice is moved, added or cancelled, plus a flag when two kids need you in two places.\n3. **Setup in a minute, no logins.** Paste a link, or snap a screenshot of any schedule. Grandparents follow along free.\n\n**Price:** $3.99/month (or $29.99/year) for the whole family, estimate.\n\n**Flow animation (4 steps)**\n1. Three team-app icons (TeamSnap, GameChanger, Heja) with a \"Copy calendar link\" tap.\n2. Paste into **KidSlate** → \"Maya · U10 Soccer\" and \"Leo · 12U Baseball\" appear in two colors.\n3. One week view fills up; a red \"overlap Sat 10:00\" flag shows.\n4. A phone lock screen gets a push: \"Leo's game moved to 11:30, Field 4.\"\n\n**Buttons**\n- Main: **\"Start for $3.99/month\"** → fake checkout screen: \"Thanks! We're not open yet. You'll be first in line, and we'll email you before anything is charged.\" (no payment taken)\n- Softer link: **\"Join waitlist\"** (email only)\n- Note under the buttons: **\"In development, join early access.\"**\n\n**Suggested ad angle:** a 10-second phone screen recording: three team apps → one color-coded week → a \"game moved\" push. Hook: \"Two kids, three team apps, one missed game? Get every game in one schedule.\" Target US parents 30–50 with youth-sports interests (TeamSnap, GameChanger, Little League, AYSO, club soccer), Android and iPhone; run in-season (now: fall soccer/basketball start).",
   "test": "Two-button validation page (below) with **\"Start for $3.99/month\"** and a softer waitlist link, plus €30–50 of Meta ads to US parents of school-age kids with youth-sports interests (TeamSnap, GameChanger, Little League, AYSO, club soccer). Bar: 100+ US visitors; >3% price clicks strong, <1% kill. Also, before building: check by hand which of TeamSnap, GameChanger, SportsEngine, LeagueApps, Heja, TeamLinkt and sportsYou give parents a subscribable feed link (an hour of work, decides how much the screenshot fallback matters).",
